---
description: Use when a task prepares repository documentation, a commit, a push, a pull request, ownership, licensing, or contribution policy. Do not use for implementation-only work that will not be delivered in this task.
alwaysApply: false
---

- Read `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `OWNERS.md`, and the active task scope
  before changing delivery or governance files. Obtain any missing GitHub
  handle, legal entity, security email, repository URL, or release policy from
  the owner rather than inferring it.
- Use `deploy-lab-git-delivery` before preparing a commit or push. A Skill
  guides the agent; Commitlint and Lefthook are the deterministic enforcement.
- Use Conventional Commits: `type(optional-scope): imperative summary`. Commit
  only the approved file scope; commit and push require explicit user approval.
- Keep third-party legal text verbatim. Update `NOTICE` when adding distributable
  third-party attributions; do not add a governance, changelog, or release
  process without an actual project need.
